  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Here is a sequence: 500, 100, 20, . . .</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain why this sequence could be a geometric sequence.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The given terms have a common ratio. \(100=\frac15\cdot 500\), and \(20=\frac15\cdot 100\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the next term? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(20 \cdot \frac15 = 4\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain how you know the next term. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Multiplying a term by the common ratio gives the next term.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
